.TH MINIT 1 "2026-02-11" "v1.1" "Custom Scripts Manual"
.SH NAME
minit \- CMake project initializer and dependency manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minit
\fIinit\fR|\fIinitialize\fR|\fInew\fR [\fB\-v\fR] \fIpath\fR [\fIpath\-options\fR]
.br
.B minit
\fIconf\fR|\fIconfigure\fR \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-add\fR \fIdep\fR [\fB\-\-static\fR] [\fB\-\-public\fR|\fB\-\-private\fR]] [\fB\-\-remove\fR \fIdep\fR]
.br
.B minit
\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minit
is a utility script for initializing and managing CMake projects. It creates structured project directories and handles dependency management through a unified interface.

.SH INIT MODE
Creates a new CMake project structure.
.TP
\fB\-\-pkg\-config\fR
Enable PkgConfig validation and tracking for all dependencies added to this project.

.SH CONF MODE
Manages dependencies for an existing CMake project.
.TP
\fB\-\-add \fIdep\fR [\fB\-\-static\fR] [\fB\-\-public\fR|\fB\-\-private\fR]
Add a dependency to the project.
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-static\fR: Forces static linking. If PkgConfig is used, it adds the \fBSTATIC\fR flag to the module check. If not, it wraps the dependency in linker-specific static flags.
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-public\fR: Links the dependency to the \fBdeps_public\fR interface. These are visible to external projects linking against this library. (Default for libraries) .
.IP \(bu 4
\fB\-\-private\fR: Links the dependency to the \fBdeps_private\fR interface. These are hidden from external projects. (Default for binaries) .
.RE

.SH DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT
Dependencies are managed via two interface targets in \fICMakeLists.txt\fR: \fBdeps_public\fR and \fBdeps_private\fR.
.PP
Use \fBconf\fR mode to insert dependencies between the \fB@DEPS_START_PUBLIC@\fR or \fB@DEPS_START_PRIVATE@\fR markers.

.SH EXAMPLES
Add a public, static dependency using PkgConfig:
.RS
.PP
minit conf ./myproject \-\-add zlib \-\-static \-\-public
.RE
.PP
Add a private dependency to a binary:
.RS
.PP
minit conf ./myproject \-\-add "Threads::Threads" \-\-private
.RE

.SH NOTES
The script uses portable \fBsed\fR commands compatible with GNU and BSD versions. For static linking without PkgConfig, the script utilizes \fB\-Wl,\-Bstatic\fR flags which may be toolchain-dependent.
